# Manifest Log — append-only completion tracking
# Format: TIMESTAMP | AGENT | STATUS | DETAILS
# 
# This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for project state.
# Every entry is immediately committed to git after writing.
#
# Status values:
#   INITIALIZED  — project created
#   INTAKE_COMPLETE — Phase 0 done, moving to research
#   RESEARCH_COMPLETE — Phase 1 done, all researchers returned
#   PLAN_APPROVED — Phase 2 done, user confirmed plan
#   STARTED — worker began a task
#   COMMITTED — worker pushed code to branch
#   DONE — task fully complete (worker shipped, or gate passed)
#   BLOCKED — worker cannot proceed (dependency or build loop)
#   REJECTED — SecArch rejected the task
#   FAIL — Tester found failures
#   ESCALATED — exceeded retry budget, user notified
#   SHIPPED — Phase 6 complete, project delivered
#
# Recovery: If a session dies, read this log + git log to reconstruct state.
# Rule: Never merge a branch whose worker has no DONE entry here.
# Rule: Every write to this file is followed by: git add + git commit
#
